msgid "Design principles of operator representations {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Designprinzipien der Operatordarstellungen {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains the common design principles and core concepts shared across all operator representations in the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module.\n"
msgstr "Dieser Leitfaden erläutert die gemeinsamen Designprinzipien und Kernkonzepte, die alle Operatordarstellungen im Modul [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") teilen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Überblick {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator representations provided by this module share several fundamental design principles:\n"
msgstr "Die von diesem Modul bereitgestellten Operatordarstellungen teilen mehrere grundlegende Designprinzipien:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Sparse data structure**](#sparse-term-representation): Operators encode only non-identity operations. The internal data layout is generally inspired by sparse matrix data formats, enabling efficient storage and computation for systems with many modes but relatively few significant contributions.\n"
msgstr "[**Dünnbesetzte Datenstruktur**](#sparse-term-representation): Operatoren kodieren nur Nicht-Identitätsoperationen. Das interne Datenlayout ist im Allgemeinen von dünnbesetzten Matrixformaten inspiriert und ermöglicht effiziente Speicherung und Berechnung für Systeme mit vielen Moden, aber relativ wenigen wesentlichen Beiträgen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Term iteration and reconstruction**](#term-iteration-and-reconstruction): Irrespective of the internal sparse storage, operators provide a consistent iteration interface, so you can inspect, filter, and transform terms without understanding the underlying data structure, then reconstruct new operators from modified terms.\n"
msgstr "[**Term-Iteration und Rekonstruktion**](#term-iteration-and-reconstruction): Unabhängig vom internen dünnbesetzten Speicher bieten Operatoren eine konsistente Iterationsschnittstelle, sodass du Terme untersuchen, filtern und transformieren kannst, ohne die zugrunde liegende Datenstruktur zu verstehen, und anschließend aus den veränderten Termen neue Operatoren rekonstruierst.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Mode-based indexing**](#mode-based-indexing): Operators use abstract mode indices to label fermionic degrees of freedom, enabling flexible mapping from physical systems to the operator representation.\n"
msgstr "[**Modenbasierte Indizierung**](#mode-based-indexing): Operatoren verwenden abstrakte Mode-Indizes, um fermionische Freiheitsgrade zu benennen, was eine flexible Abbildung von physikalischen Systemen auf die Operatordarstellung ermöglicht.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Term grouping and commutation relationships**](#term-grouping): Operators natively support grouping information that associates terms with group indices. This enables optimizations and physical structure preservation without requiring separate data structures. See the [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) for practical usage.\n"
msgstr "[**Termgruppierung und Kommutationsbeziehungen**](#term-grouping): Operatoren unterstützen nativ Gruppierungsinformationen, die Terme mit Gruppenindizes verknüpfen. Das ermöglicht Optimierungen und den Erhalt der physikalischen Struktur, ohne separate Datenstrukturen zu benötigen. Die praktische Verwendung findest du im [Gruppierungsleitfaden](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Arithmetic and mathematical operations**](#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations): All operators implement a consistent set of arithmetic operations (such as addition, multiplication, and composition) and mathematical functions by using the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, enabling uniform code across different operator types.\n"
msgstr "[**Arithmetische und mathematische Operationen**](#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations): Alle Operatoren implementieren über das Protokoll [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") einen konsistenten Satz arithmetischer Operationen (wie Addition, Multiplikation und Komposition) und mathematischer Funktionen, was einheitlichen Code über verschiedene Operatortypen hinweg ermöglicht.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Operator term ordering and normal forms**](#operator-term-ordering): Mathematically equivalent operators can have very different representations and behavior in quantum algorithms. All operator representations support various normal forms (based on algebra-specific commutation relations) to achieve canonical, predictable, and optimizable operator representations.\n"
msgstr "[**Termreihenfolge und Normalformen von Operatoren**](#operator-term-ordering): Mathematisch äquivalente Operatoren können in Quantenalgorithmen sehr unterschiedliche Darstellungen und ein sehr unterschiedliches Verhalten haben. Alle Operatordarstellungen unterstützen verschiedene Normalformen (basierend auf algebraspezifischen Kommutationsrelationen), um kanonische, vorhersagbare und optimierbare Operatordarstellungen zu erreichen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sparse-term-representation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sparse data structure {#sparse-data-structure}"
msgstr "Dünnbesetzte Datenstruktur {#sparse-data-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operators use a **sparse representation** where only non-identity operations are tracked. Each non-identity operation consists of a **coefficient** (complex number) and a **sequence of actions** on specific modes.\n"
msgstr "Alle Operatoren verwenden eine **dünnbesetzte Darstellung**, in der nur Nicht-Identitätsoperationen verfolgt werden. Jede Nicht-Identitätsoperation besteht aus einem **Koeffizienten** (komplexe Zahl) und einer **Folge von Aktionen** auf bestimmten Moden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach dramatically reduces memory usage and computation time, especially for systems with many modes but relatively few significant contributions. By encoding only non-identity operations, operations focus only on what matters, enabling work with large systems that would be infeasible with dense representations. Additionally, operators naturally scale to any number of modes; an operator acting on modes `{0, 1}` works unchanged in systems with many more modes since unaffected modes are implicitly identity.\n"
msgstr "Dieser Ansatz reduziert Speicherbedarf und Rechenzeit drastisch, besonders bei Systemen mit vielen Moden, aber relativ wenigen wesentlichen Beiträgen. Indem nur Nicht-Identitätsoperationen kodiert werden, konzentrieren sich die Operationen nur auf das, was zählt, und ermöglichen die Arbeit mit großen Systemen, die mit dichten Darstellungen nicht machbar wären. Außerdem skalieren Operatoren natürlich auf beliebig viele Moden; ein Operator, der auf die Moden `{0, 1}` wirkt, funktioniert unverändert in Systemen mit viel mehr Moden, da nicht betroffene Moden implizit die Identität sind.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Identical terms are preserved separately during arithmetic operations and must be explicitly combined if needed.\n"
msgstr "Identische Terme bleiben bei arithmetischen Operationen getrennt erhalten und müssen bei Bedarf explizit zusammengeführt werden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internal storage format {#internal-storage-format}"
msgstr "Internes Speicherformat {#internal-storage-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internally, operators are stored in arrays inspired by sparse matrix data formats:\n"
msgstr "Intern werden Operatoren in Arrays gespeichert, die von dünnbesetzten Matrixformaten inspiriert sind:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Coefficients array**: The complex coefficient for each term\n"
msgstr "**Koeffizienten-Array**: Der komplexe Koeffizient jedes Terms\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mode indices array**: The fermionic modes that each action acts upon\n"
msgstr "**Mode-Index-Array**: Die fermionischen Moden, auf die jede Aktion wirkt\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Boundaries array**: Indices marking where each term’s modes begin and end in the mode array\n"
msgstr "**Grenzen-Array**: Indizes, die markieren, wo die Moden jedes Terms im Mode-Array beginnen und enden\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Additional arrays might be present depending on the operator type. For example, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") instances include an **actions array** of booleans that specifies the type of fermionic action acting on the respective mode index. In contrast, the `MajoranaOperator` class does not require this distinction since it encodes that information in the parity of the mode index. See the API documentation for your operator type to understand the full storage format.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Wichtig\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Je nach Operatortyp können zusätzliche Arrays vorhanden sein. [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")-Instanzen enthalten zum Beispiel ein **Aktions-Array** aus Booleans, das den Typ der fermionischen Aktion auf dem jeweiligen Mode-Index angibt. Die Klasse `MajoranaOperator` benötigt diese Unterscheidung dagegen nicht, da sie diese Information in der Parität des Mode-Index kodiert. Das vollständige Speicherformat findest du in der API-Dokumentation deines Operatortyps.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following examples show how these arrays are organized. First is a direct construction using the sparse arrays:\n"
msgstr "Die folgenden Beispiele zeigen, wie diese Arrays organisiert sind. Zuerst eine direkte Konstruktion mit den dünnbesetzten Arrays:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operators directly using sparse arrays\n"
"    >>> # First operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0],\n"
"    ...     actions=[True, False],\n"
"    ...     modes=[0, 1],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0],\n"
"    ...     actions=[True, False],\n"
"    ...     modes=[2, 3],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Combine the sparse operators\n"
"    >>> op1 += op2\n"
"    >>> print(format(op1))\n"
"      1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+0 -1)\n"
"      1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+2 -3)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct first operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 1};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct first operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 1};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff2[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions2[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes2[2] = {2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries2[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op2 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff2, actions2, modes2, boundaries2);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff2[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions2[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes2[2] = {2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries2[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op2 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff2, actions2, modes2, boundaries2);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Combine the sparse operators. There is no in-place add in the C API, so\n"
"    // the sum is a new operator that the caller owns.\n"
